WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.534
-Our next guest has his stand-up special,

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.868
"Downhill Ever Since," available on YouTube.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.400
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.734
please welcome the very funny Raanan Hershberg.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.400
♪♪

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.634
-Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:21.934
How are you all doing? Huh?

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.868
[ Cheers and applause ] Great.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:28.267
So I've been sober now for five years. Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.334
[ Applause ]

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:31.634
It's actually been a couple weeks,

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.467
but it feels like five years.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.501
[ Laughter ] No. It's been a while.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:36.667
But even when I wasn't sober,

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:38.200
there were some drugs I never did.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.334
Like, I hate edibles. They're my least favorite drug.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.734
'Cause every edible instruction is always the same

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.100
and it's always nonsense.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.801
It's always someone handing you a cookie and being like,

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.934
"Only do half!"

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:56.634
"Do not do more than half! Just half!"

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:58.133
It's like, "Excuse me.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:01.167
I never had half a cookie in my life."

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:05.133
Never!

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.467
[ Applause ]

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:11.701
I've either had zero cookies or all the cookies.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:14.200
There's no in-between with cookies.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.167
If you want me to have half of something,

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.200
how about you don't put the marijuana in a dessert?

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.100
How about that? Right?

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.334
Don't put it in a brownie or a gummy.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:24.367
I'll do half a weed carrot.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.667
Yeah, I don't want to brag,

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.801
but I can do half a carrot, no problem.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:34.200
I never once had half a carrot and been like,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.467
"Get this away from me before I eat the whole thing!"

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.133
Now that I'm sober, I have no tolerance.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.501
That's what happens.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:45.067
I used to do drugs till the dawn.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:48.200
Now if I see someone drinking coffee after 2:00,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.267
I'm like, "Take a look at Keith Richards over here."

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:55.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:59.467
"What is that? Cold brew? Are you out of your mind?

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.601
Do you need an intervention right now?"

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.734
But I'm also getting older. You know, I'm 37.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.501
A lot of people think I'm younger

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:08.434
'cause I've had so few accomplishments.

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:09.868
But I'm --

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.601
And it's hard to get old, too.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.334
It really is. Especially in America.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:16.968
It is hard to get old.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:18.968
Once you turn 75 in America,

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:20.901
you do not have a lot of options.

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.133
You really don't.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.067
You can either be put into a nursing home

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:27.734
or run every aspect of government.

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:29.868
Yeah.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:33.234
[ Applause ]

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.467
Those are the only options.

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:37.000
All of you have to make a choice at 75.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.534
Do you want to play bingo all day long

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:42.334
or do you want to pass legislation

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:46.334
that will have no effect on your life whatsoever?

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.767
I thought as I get older,

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:51.834
I'd get less anxious, and that is not the case.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:55.167
I'm a huge hypochondriac, and my twin sister is, too,

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.901
but she's, like, a cocky kind.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.968
Like, she recently saw a couple moles on my back.

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:00.334
And this is how cocky she is.

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:03.501
She said, "A couple of those moles look suspicious,

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:06.267
but you should probably get a second opinion."

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.901
I was like, "No offense, but I do not consider

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:14.300
what you just said a first opinion."

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:18.300
"Who do you think you are?" The gall.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.501
You know how crappy that'd be if I went to my doctor

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:23.534
and I was like, "I was just with my twin sister,

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:28.934
and now I'm here for a second opinion.

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:31.601
And after you, I'm gonna talk to my mailman,

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.667
and he's gonna break the tie.

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:37.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.200
Why are you crying, Doctor?"

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.934
Anyway, she was a little insulted

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.601
'cause she's a dermatologist.

00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:46.100
But I still feel strongly...

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:51.100
...that she was being condescending!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.801
My mom is getting up there. My mom is in her 70s.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.634
And she's kind of losing it. Like, recently, one of

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.000
my paychecks accidentally got mailed to her.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.901
And she had to deposit it into my banking mobile account.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.267
And this is 100% true.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.167
I'm on the phone with her, and she goes,

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.133
"Alright. To get into your account,

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.601
there's a security question!"

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:10.067
And I'm like, "What's the security question?"

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:15.100
And she goes, "What city was your mother born in?"

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:24.033
"Are you telling me I'm adopted or that you have dementia?

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.634
What's going on?"

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:29.400
Now isn't it terrifying to think that in only ten years --

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.234
in only ten years, she'll be ready to run for president?

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:36.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:38.834
My mom loves to speak in clichés.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.834
She said my favorite cliché the other day.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:46.434
She said, "I can't believe it's already January!"

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:51.534
Really?

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.467
That's the thing

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:57.634
in these last insane couple of years

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:01.133
that you have trouble believing?

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:04.667
That's the part, out of all the improbable stuff

00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:07.167
that has happened?!

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.701
Kanye West ran for president!

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:13.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:17.467
That wasn't a dream. That happened.

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:21.000
Rudolph Giuliani got brought down by Borat.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:25.734
A fictional character.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:29.100
That's like Austin Powers arresting Mike Pence.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.934
There was a coup on the Capitol

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.400
that looked like if the French Revolution

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.133
was re-enacted by Carnival Cruise passengers.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:42.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:45.167
And out of all that, the thing my mom

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.200
has to pinch her cheek about

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.501
is that time -- are you ready for this --

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:52.767
moves forward.

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.000
I can't wait till aliens land.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.167
I'm gonna be like, "Mom, can you believe this?"

00:05:56.167 --> 00:06:01.133
And she's gonna be like, "I know! Hanukkah already?!"

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:03.100
I'm Raanan Hershberg. You've all been so wonderful.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.801
Thank you so much.

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:07.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.868
-Fantastic, dude.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.334
♪♪

00:06:10.334 --> 00:06:12.567
Raanan Hershberg!

00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:15.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:18.300
"Downhill Ever Since" is available right now on YouTube.

